"lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 16 <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Quadr">Q</ref> | forisfactus [<hi rend="italic">alleinsteh.</hi>] <hi rend="italic">wer <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:durch"><abbr>durch</abbr></ref> Verbrechen Leibesstrafe</hi> [<hi rend="italic">Tod</hi>] <hi rend="italic">verdient hat, <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:auch"><abbr>auch</abbr></ref> <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:vor"><abbr>vor</abbr></ref> der Verhaftung</hi> [<hi rend="italic">zu eng <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:missversteht"><abbr>missversteht</abbr></ref></hi> Rubr <ref type="lawCode" target="law:retr">retr</ref>: reus lege dampnatus] <ref type="lawCode" target="law:ECf">ECf</ref> 18 | ~ se ipsum <hi rend="italic">sein Leben v.</hi> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 2 <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Quadr">Q</ref>. Cons, hine sylfne forwyrce <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:ubersetzend"><abbr>übsnd</abbr></ref>;</hi> erga Deum <hi rend="italic">sich versündigen</hi> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Episc">Episc</ref> 8 <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Quadr">Q</ref>, forwyrcean hi sylfe wið God <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:ubersetzend"><abbr>übsnd</abbr></ref>;</hi> se ipsos -ciunt <hi rend="italic">machen sich schuldig</hi> (<hi rend="italic">eigenes Wergeld zu zahlen</hi>) In Cn III 46</dictScrap>
